# Exhaustive switches

Use `never`, `assertNever`, `invariant`, or an equivalent throw only for a
program-owned union closed by construction or boundary normalization. Static
types do not close raw RPC, protobuf, IPC, persisted, deep-link, plugin, or
other independently versioned values at runtime.

Long-lived client display paths map well-formed newer values to an explicit
renderable `unknown` / `unsupported` domain arm; malformed values and strict
control inputs return a typed rejection. Exhaustively switch only on that
closed domain union, never on the raw external value.

Query, transport, and command failures remain errors in their owning channels.
